let __v_247 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Ask for one example with a time and a place - 'when was the last time?' - instead of arguing about all of you. A real instance tells you what to change; a verdict does not.\",\"Take the grain of truth and say what you would like instead: 'you're right that I've been on my phone at dinner - I'll put it down.' That ends it faster than a defence does, and it does not mean agreeing with all of it.\",\"Ask what they would like more of rather than whether they are right: 'what would a good evening look like for you?' That is a question with an answer, and a verdict is not.\",\"Say it back before you answer, so you both know what is being said: 'so you feel like I'm not really here - is that it?' A fair amount of these turn out to be about one bad week.\",\"Give it a hearing without signing up to all of it: 'some of that lands and some of it doesn't - can we talk about the bit that matters most?' Then do that one thing.\"]}")?;
