let __v_248 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Then you have said it, which is the hard half. Say the same sentence again next time, in the same words - a line that comes back identical is what makes it a rule rather than a mood, and it is the explaining that gives them something to argue with.\",\"The first time is usually the one that gets argued with, so say it once more the same way and then let it sit. Nothing changes in the moment; what changes is that they now know what you will say.\",\"A quiet reply to that is normal, and it is not the answer yet. Hold the line exactly as you put it - 'I can't do that' - and leave the door open for the next time: 'ask me again about Saturday and I'll say yes'.\"]}")?;
